There is a reeaaaally simple solution to this...
If Markus doesn't already have an attack skill that's different from the default. Copy and paste the default attack skill (the first one in the skill database) and change the formula to this:
Code:
c = a.atk - b.def; b.gainHp(c); c
Then go into Markus in the actor database and set his attack skill to the one you just made. This works because the enemy gains the same amount of health as damage they are dealt BEFORE they are refreshed and checked for death (0 health). Resulting in a net damage worth of zero while still showing damage results corresponding to the original formula damage. It can't even kill an enemy with a max hp of 1. I thought it wouldn't work initially because I tried the same thing but instead of gaining health I gave the enemy a 0%* physical damage state and it didn't work. RPGM is weird under the hood.
Although I do have to question your intentions with Markus healing you on an occasion. I thought you would be trying to minimize all gameplay differences versions to record only the psychological differences between versions, and having an actual worthwhile difference would be problematic. I would suggest just having Markus apply a fake buff state instead.
Edit: Yeah I was HELLA wrong lmao. The formula thing doesn't work at all. The reason I thought I did was because I made a mini plugin that solves your problem and forgot about it before coming up with the formula thing. But at least I know it works lol.
JavaScript:
/*:
 *
 * @target MZ
 * @plugindesc For actors whose attacks are only visual.
 * @author Lowrell Lovelace
 *
 */

(() => {

let targetActorId = 5;

const _Game_Action_prototype_executeDamage = Game_Action.prototype.executeDamage;
Game_Action.prototype.executeDamage = function(target, value) {

    let subject = this.subject();

    if (subject.isActor() && subject._actorId === targetActorId && target.isEnemy()) {
        target._hp += value;
    }
    _Game_Action_prototype_executeDamage.call(this, target, value);
};

})();
Since you never worked with Javascript I'm gonna give you a quick tutorial. Just copy and paste the code snippet into notepad and change the 5 in "let targetActorId = 5;" to Markus' actor id which you can see left to his name in the actors database. Save it as "whatevernameyouwant.js" the .js part is really important. And save it in the \js\plugins folder of your game. Then open RPG Maker MZ and then click on the plugin manager, click on a column, click under "Name:" and find the plugin you just saved. Click okay on everything and save. No matter how much damage Markus deals he can never kill an enemy.
I know it sounds complicated at first but this is probably the easiest and least troublesome option I can offer you.

